   "M\u00f6bius Energy of Thick Knots",
   "Eric J. Rawdon 2"
  ],
  "abstract": "The M\u00a8 obius energy of a knot is an energy functional for smoot h curves based on an idea of self-repelling. If a knot has a thick tubular neigh borhood, we would intuitively expect the energy to be low. In this paper, we giv e explicit bounds for energy in terms of the ropelength of the knot, i.e. the ratio o f the length of a thickest tube to its radius.",
